    ns1:description """Kmer counting step, can run alone or as part of a combined workflow for large genome assembly. \r
\r
* What it does: Estimates genome size and heterozygosity based on counts of kmers\r
* Inputs: One set of short reads: e.g. R1.fq.gz\r
* Outputs: GenomeScope graphs\r
* Tools used: Meryl, GenomeScope\r
* Input parameters: None required\r
* Workflow steps: The tool meryl counts kmers in the input reads (k=21), then converts this into a histogram. GenomeScope: runs a model on the histogram; reports estimates. k-mer size set to 21. \r
* Options: Use a different kmer counting tool. e.g. khmer.\r
\r
\r
Infrastructure_deployment_metadata: Galaxy Australia (Galaxy)""" ;
