    ns1:description """# Snakemake workflow: FAIR CRCC - send data\r
\r
[![Snakemake](https://img.shields.io/badge/snakemake-≥6.3.0-brightgreen.svg)](https://snakemake.github.io)\r
[![GitHub actions status](https://github.com/crs4/fair-crcc-send-data/workflows/Tests/badge.svg?branch=main)](https://github.com/crs4/fair-crcc-send-data/actions?query=branch%3Amain+workflow%3ATests)\r
\r
\r
A Snakemake workflow for securely sharing Crypt4GH-encrypted sensitive data from\r
the [CRC\r
Cohort](https://www.bbmri-eric.eu/scientific-collaboration/colorectal-cancer-cohort/)\r
to a destination approved through a successful [access\r
request](https://www.bbmri-eric.eu/services/access-policies/).\r
\r
The recommendation is to create a directory for the request that has been\r
approved;  it will be used as the working directory for the run.  Copy there the\r
recipient's crypt4gh key and prepare the run configuration.  The configuration\r
will specify the repository, the destination of the data, and the list of\r
files/directories to transfer.\r
\r
\r
## What's the CRC Cohort?\r
\r
The CRC Cohort is a collection of clinical data and digital high-resolution\r
digital pathology images pertaining to tumor cases.  The collection has been\r
assembled from a number of participating biobanks and other partners through the\r
[ADOPT BBMRI-ERIC](https://www.bbmri-eric.eu/scientific-collaboration/adopt-bbmri-eric/) project.\r
\r
Researchers interested in using the data for science can file an application for\r
access.  If approved, the part of the dataset required for the planned and\r
approved work can be copied to the requester's selected secure storage location\r
(using this workflow).\r
\r
\r
## Usage\r
\r
### Example\r
\r
    mkdir request_1234 &amp;&amp; cd request_1234\r
    # Now write the configuration, specifying crypt4gh keys, destination and files to send.\r
    # Finally, execute workflow.\r
    snakemake --snakefile ../fair-crcc-send-data/workflow/Snakefile --profile ../profile/ --configfile config.yml --use-singularity --cores\r
\r
\r
#### Run configuration example\r
\r
```\r
recipient_key: ./recipient_key\r
repository:\r
  path: "/mnt/rbd/data/sftp/fair-crcc/"\r
  private_key: bbmri-key\r
  public_key: bbmri-key.pub\r
sources:\r
  glob_extension: ".tiff.c4gh"\r
  items:\r
  - some/directory/to/glob\r
  - another/individual/file.tiff.c4gh\r
destination:\r
  type: "S3"\r
  root_path: "my-bucket/prefix/"\r
  connection:  # all elements will be passed to the selected snakemake remote provider\r
    access_key_id: "MYACCESSKEY"\r
    secret_access_key: "MYSECRET"\r
    host: http://localhost:9000\r
    verify: false # don't verify ssl certificates\r
```\r
\r
\r
TODO\r
\r
The usage of this workflow is described in the [Snakemake Workflow Catalog](https://snakemake.github.io/snakemake-workflow-catalog/?usage=crs4%2Ffair-crcc-send-data).\r
\r
If you use this workflow in a paper, don't forget to give credits to the authors by citing the URL of this (original) fair-crcc-send-datasitory and its DOI (see above).\r
""" ;
