<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/484?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow,
        ns1:SoftwareSourceCode ;
    dcterms:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE/" ;
    ns1:creator <#The%20Workflows%20and%20Distributed%20Computing%20Team%20(https://www.bsc.es/discover-bsc/organisation/scientific-structure/workflows-and-distributed-computing)>,
        <https://workflowhub.eu/people/556> ;
    ns1:dateCreated "2023-05-30T07:23:13Z"^^ns1:Date ;
    ns1:dateModified "2023-10-28T07:59:47Z"^^ns1:Date ;
    ns1:description """**Name:** Matrix Multiplication  \r
**Contact Person:** support-compss@bsc.es  \r
**Access Level:** public  \r
**License Agreement:** Apache2  \r
**Platform:** COMPSs  \r
\r
# Description\r
Matrix multiplication is a binary operation that takes a pair of matrices and produces another matrix.\r
\r
If A is an n×m matrix and B is an m×p matrix, the result AB of their multiplication is an n×p matrix defined only if the number of columns m in A is equal to the number of rows m in B. When multiplying A and B, the elements of the rows in A are multiplied with corresponding columns in B.\r
\r
In this implementation, A and B are square matrices (same number of rows and columns), and so it is the result matrix C. Each matrix is divided in N blocks of M doubles. The multiplication of two blocks is done by a multiply task method with a simple three-nested-loop implementation. When executed with COMPSs, the main program generates N^3^ tasks arranged as N^2^ chains of N tasks in the dependency graph.\r
\r
# Versions\r
There are three versions of Matrix Multiplication, depending on the data types used to store the blocks.\r
## Version 1\r
''files'', where the matrix blocks are stored in files.\r
## Version 2\r
''objects'', where the matrix blocks are represented by objects.\r
## Version 3\r
''arrays'', where the matrix blocks are stored in arrays.\r
\r
# Execution instructions\r
Usage:\r
```\r
runcompss matmul.files.Matmul numberOfBlocks blockSize\r
runcompss matmul.objects.Matmul numberOfBlocks blockSize\r
runcompss matmul.arrays.Matmul numberOfBlocks blockSize\r
``` \r
\r
where:\r
  * numberOfBlocks: Number of blocks inside each matrix\r
  * blockSize: Size of each block\r
\r
\r
# Execution Example\r
```\r
runcompss matmul.objects.Matmul 16 4\r
runcompss matmul.files.Matmul 16 4\r
runcompss matmul.arrays.Matmul 16 4  \r
```\r
\r
# Build\r
## Option 1: Native java\r
```\r
cd ~/tutorial_apps/java/matmul/; javac src/main/java/matmul/*/*.java\r
cd src/main/java/; jar cf matmul.jar matmul/\r
cd ../../../; mv src/main/java/matmul.jar jar/\r
```\r
\r
## Option 2: Maven\r
```\r
cd ~/tutorial_apps/java/matmul/\r
mvn clean package\r
```\r
""" ;
