    ns1:description """**Name:** Word Count  \r
**Contact Person**: support-compss@bsc.es  \r
**Access Level**: public  \r
**License Agreement**: Apache2  \r
**Platform**: COMPSs  \r
\r
# Description\r
Wordcount is an application that counts the number of words for a given set of files.\r
\r
To allow parallelism the file is divided in blocks that are treated separately and merged afterwards.\r
\r
Results are printed to a Pickle binary file, so they can be checked using: python -mpickle result.txt\r
\r
This example also shows how to manually add input or output datasets to the workflow provenance recording (using the 'input' and 'output' terms in the ro-crate-info.yaml file).\r
\r
# Execution instructions\r
Usage:\r
```\r
runcompss --lang=python $(pwd)/application_sources/src/wordcount_blocks.py filePath resultPath blockSize\r
```\r
\r
where:\r
* filePath: Absolute path of the file to parse\r
* resultPath: Absolute path to the result file\r
* blockSize: Size of each block. The lower the number, the more tasks will be generated in the workflow\r
\r
# Execution Examples\r
```\r
runcompss --lang=python $(pwd)/application_sources/src/wordcount_blocks.py $(pwd)/dataset/data/compss.txt result.txt 300\r
runcompss $(pwd)/application_sources/src/wordcount_blocks.py $(pwd)/dataset/data/compss.txt result.txt 300\r
python -m pycompss $(pwd)/application_sources/src/wordcount.py $(pwd)/dataset/data/compss.txt result.txt 300\r
```\r
\r
# Build\r
No build is required\r
""" ;
